  "description": "Stuxnet — a computer weapon built by states, discovered by accident, never officially owned — is reconstructed through investigators and increasingly nervous anonymous sources. It shows the moment warfare went deniable and software-based: attacks with no return address, precedents set in secret, and rules of engagement that still don't exist.\n\nA documentary focused on Stuxnet, a piece of self-replicating computer malware that the U.S. and Israel unleashed to destroy a key part of an Iranian nuclear facility, and which ultimately spread beyond its intended target.",
